	(text "ARM high: Q2 on, ARM_G pulled down, Q1 on, V_SW = V_PROT.\nARM low or floating: R23 holds Q2 off, R20 holds Q1 off, V_SW dead.\nA Pi reset returns GPIO 25 to an input with a pull-down: the loads\nlose power through every reboot. Power-on safety: spec section 5.\nD3 clamps Vgs: at 24 V the R20/R21 divider gives -23 V, D3 holds -12 V.\nAt a 5 V supply Vgs is only about -4.0 V: spec section 4.4.\nC13 not fitted: 10 nF to 47 nF slows Q1 turn-on if arming dips +5V.\nD4: when Q1 opens with coils energised, their current flows through D4.\nJP8: no shunt. Fitted, it bypasses the arm switch. Test only."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 170.18 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "96600ef1-ab83-5cbf-b71e-e87e000e50f8")
	)
	(text "To verify: Q1 pin order assumed for TO-220 as\n1 gate, 2 drain, 3 source (IRF9540N style).\nQ2 2N3904, TO-92: 1 emitter, 2 base, 3 collector.\nCheck both against the parts bought."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 76.2 190.5 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "dfec9c65-4e25-5f08-93eb-652743472bea")
	)
